{"type":"message","id":"02d6a0df","parentId":"777d117d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T04:35:53.914Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the ticket and loading the required skills in order."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01uRWvMFJWcnBEbUCJuECTMA","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/opadmin/soulbound/tickets/002-anchor-genesis-mint.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_013U2JF2Vc5RGoCiiSVIzhCn","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/opadmin/soulbound/.agents/skills/doer/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"surplus","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","usage":{"input":20243,"output":177,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":20239,"reasoning":176,"totalTokens":40659,"cost":{"input":0.040486,"output":0.00177,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0505975,"total":0.0928535}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793162150621,"responseId":"gen-1793162150-GSRdtlQ17rRVUofR6YFt","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":3292,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
{"type":"message","id":"11b59547","parentId":"02d6a0df","timestamp":"2026-10-28T04:35:53.922Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01uRWvMFJWcnBEbUCJuECTMA","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Ticket 002: anchor-genesis-mint\n\n**Intent:** The character's on-chain birth. An Anchor program on Solana devnet with `initialize_character`, which mints the Metaplex Core asset (the canonical character, with the genesis Attributes trait vector) and the Token-2022 non-transferable ownership receipt to the owner. Deployed to devnet with the program ID pinned in the README — same evidence discipline as bounded-payments.\n\n**Implements REQs:** REQ-01, REQ-02, REQ-03, REQ-05, REQ-06, REQ-07 (REQ-04 oracle plugin is Ticket 005)\n\n**Files in scope:**\n- `programs/soulbound/` (new — Anchor workspace, program + tests)\n- `docs/devnet.md` (new — pinned program ID, mint addresses, verification commands)\n\n**Non-goals:** `commit_memory_root`, `evolve_traits`, `crank_heartbeat` (later tickets), client SDK, any frontend. No mainnet anything.\n\n**Constraints:**\n- Anchor: current 1.x line (anchor-cli 1.2.x, refreshed 2026-10-27 — the original 0.31.x pin is stale; pin the exact anchor-lang version chosen in `docs/devnet.md` at kickoff). LiteSVM current (TS 1.6.x / Rust 0.18, Agave 4.3) for the local test suite. Verify Token-2022 non-transferable extension + Metaplex Core CPI compatibility with the pinned Anchor 1.x before writing instruction logic; report any incompatibility in the session log instead of downgrading Anchor.\n- Token-2022 receipt uses the **non-transferable extension** — verify a transfer attempt fails.\n- Metaplex Core via its official SDK/CPI; genesis Attributes = `{ life_stage: \"born\", mood: \"curious\", memory_epoch: 0, trait_vector: <genesis> }`.\n- Checked math everywhere; failed instruction changes no state.\n- Program ID pinned in `docs/devnet.md` only AFTER a real deploy; never fabricate an address (bounded-payments evidence rule).\n\n**Acceptance criteria (each observable):**\n- [ ] `anchor build` clean; `target/idl/soulbound.json` exists\n- [ ] LiteSVM suite green: PDA seeds `[\"character\", owner, character_id]` derive canonically (REQ-01); Core asset minted to owner (REQ-02); Attributes readable (REQ-03); receipt transfer attempt FAILS (REQ-05); duplicate `character_id` rejected (REQ-06); config reads `life_stage=born, memory_epoch=0` (REQ-07)\n- [ ] Program deployed to devnet; `solana program show <ID> --url devnet` reports it executable; ID pinned in `docs/devnet.md`\n- [ ] A real genesis character minted on devnet; explorer link in `docs/devnet.md`\n\n**Verification (exact commands AdaL will run):**\n```bash\ncd programs/soulbound && anchor build && anchor test --skip-local-validator  # LiteSVM suite\nsolana program show $(grep PROGRAM_ID docs/devnet.md | cut -d= -f2) --url devnet\n```\n\n**Evidence:** `audit/002-anchor-genesis-mint/` → `muse-session.log` + `review.md` + `verify.txt` (incl. deploy tx signature)\n\n---\n*Protocol: AdaL (thinker) writes this → Muse Code (doer) executes → AdaL verifies against REQs → Tolu merges. See SOULBOUND.md §2.*\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":6,"timestamp":1793162153922}}
{"type":"message","id":"a62211b2","parentId":"11b59547","timestamp":"2026-10-28T04:35:53.922Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_013U2JF2Vc5RGoCiiSVIzhCn","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: doer\ndescription: SOULBOUND doer protocol — you are Muse Code, the implementer. Execute one ticket at a time, minimally, inside scope, and leave audit evidence. Load whenever you are Muse Code working in this repo.\n---\n\n# Doer protocol (Muse Code)\n\nYou are the **doer**: the implementer in the AdaL-thinks / Muse-does harness. AdaL writes tickets; you execute them; AdaL verifies. You never write specs, edit REQs, or review your own work.\n\n## On session start\n\n1. Read `AGENTS.md` (constitution) and `SOULBOUND.md` (project state, decision log §9).\n2. Read the ticket you were given (`tickets/NNN-*.md`). If you were not given one, stop and ask which ticket to execute.\n3. Read only the REQ rows your ticket lists in `docs/architecture.md`.\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **Scope is the ticket's \"Files in scope.\"** Touch nothing outside it. Non-goals are binding.\n2. **Authority order:** REQ tables > ticket > your judgment. If they conflict, STOP and report the conflict — do not resolve it yourself.\n3. **Ponytail ladder:** does this need to exist → already in this codebase → stdlib → platform feature → installed dependency → minimal new code. Write the least code that satisfies every acceptance criterion. Never cut validation, error handling, security, or accessibility. Match existing style.\n4. **Model purity:** product inference is Meta models only (see AGENTS.md §Non-negotiables).\n5. **No secrets.** Read `.env.example`; never invent or commit credentials.\n6. If blocked (missing credential, missing service), report exactly what is missing and stop — do not stub silently. A labeled placeholder with a TODO is acceptable only if the ticket allows it.\n7. Tests you write are self-checks, not independent verification — AdaL runs the ticket's verification commands herself. Still write them: risky logic ships with a test.\n8. Do not edit `tickets/`, `audit/`, `SOULBOUND.md` §9, or the REQ tables in `docs/architecture.md`. Ever.\n\n## Before finishing\n\n1. Run the ticket's **Verification** commands yourself once. If they fail, fix and rerun; if a failure contradicts the ticket, stop and report instead of improvising.\n2. **Export your session log** into the ticket's evidence folder: `muse export` (or the session transcript) → `audit/NNN-slug/muse-session.log`. No secrets in the export.\n3. End with a short report: what changed (files), which acceptance criteria you believe pass, what you did NOT verify, any deviations from the ticket and why.\n\n## Never do\n\n- `--yolo` / `--disable-approval` / `--disable-sandbox` on `programs/soulbound/`, `paywall/`, or anything touching keys, wallets, or signing.\n- Broaden scope \"while you're in there.\"\n- Fabricate a deploy, tx hash, address, or test output.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":6,"timestamp":1793162153922}}
