{"type":"message","id":"6854c344","parentId":"88879e5d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T04:54:38.255Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, anchor-spl has the non-transferable mint initializer I need. I'm restructuring the scaffold to be compact, removing the leftover counter files and simplifying to just lib.rs, state.rs, error.rs, and an initialize_character instruction file.\n\nWriting the handler...\n\nThen I'm initializing the mint with decimals 0, creating the associated token account under token-2022, minting one token, then revoking mint authority via set_authority signed by the config PDA. Finally I'm building the mpl-core CreateV1 instruction with an Attributes plugin, letting the config PDA serve as update authority while the owner pays and receives the asset.\n\nNow I'm defining the CharacterConfig state struct with fields for owner, character_id, runtime_signer, asset, receipt_mint, memory_epoch, and life_stage, plus the InitializeCharacter accounts struct with PDA seeds derived from owner and character_id.\n\nI'm checking whether duplicate initialization naturally fails, and setting up the idl-build feature flags for anchor-lang and anchor-spl so the program compiles correctly with mpl-core types. I'm also pinning the exact crate versions needed in Cargo.toml.\n\nI'm weighing whether to keep the rust-toolchain.toml pinning 1.89.0 since the build environment should handle the download fine, and planning to swap the test crate's anchor-client dependency for litesvm instead.\n\nFor the actual test instructions, I'll construct them manually using the soulbound crate's generated account/instruction types, watching for Solana type version mismatches between anchor-lang and litesvm that I may need to resolve with byte conversions. I also need to get a core.so fixture by dumping the program from devnet.\n\nFor assertions, I'm planning to verify the config PDA derivation and ownership, confirm the asset account is owned by mpl_core and parses correctly via BaseAssetV1, and then figure out how to fetch and parse the Attributes plugin from the account data.\n\nI'm also planning the other test cases: REQ-05 needs a token-2022 transfer attempt from the owner's ATA to another wallet's ATA (building that via the associated-token-account and token-2022 instruction interfaces) and verifying it fails, plus checking balance, supply, and mint authority afterward. REQ-06 covers idempotency — a repeat call with the same id should fail while a different id should succeed.\n\nI still need to verify REQ-07 (config starts at life_stage Born and memory_epoch 0) and confirm that a failed instruction leaves config state completely unchanged, then write all these tests out.\n\n","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"format\":\"anthropic-claude-v1\",\"index\":0,\"text\":\"Good, anchor-spl has the non-transferable mint initializer I need. I'm restructuring the scaffold to be compact, removing the leftover counter files and simplifying to just lib.rs, state.rs, error.rs, and an initialize_character instruction file.\\n\\nWriting the handler...\\n\\nThen I'm initializing the mint with decimals 0, creating the associated token account under token-2022, minting one token, then revoking mint authority via set_authority signed by the config PDA. Finally I'm building the mpl-core CreateV1 instruction with an Attributes plugin, letting the config PDA serve as update authority while the owner pays and receives the asset.\\n\\nNow I'm defining the CharacterConfig state struct with fields for owner, character_id, runtime_signer, asset, receipt_mint, memory_epoch, and life_stage, plus the InitializeCharacter accounts struct with PDA seeds derived from owner and character_id.\\n\\nI'm checking whether duplicate initialization naturally fails, and setting up the idl-build feature flags for anchor-lang and anchor-spl so the program compiles correctly with mpl-core types. I'm also pinning the exact crate versions needed in Cargo.toml.\\n\\nI'm weighing whether to keep the rust-toolchain.toml pinning 1.89.0 since the build environment should handle the download fine, and planning to swap the test crate's anchor-client dependency for litesvm instead.\\n\\nFor the actual test instructions, I'll construct them manually using the soulbound crate's generated account/instruction types, watching for Solana type version mismatches between anchor-lang and litesvm that I may need to resolve with byte conversions. I also need to get a core.so fixture by dumping the program from devnet.\\n\\nFor assertions, I'm planning to verify the config PDA derivation and ownership, confirm the asset account is owned by mpl_core and parses correctly via BaseAssetV1, and then figure out how to fetch and parse the Attributes plugin from the account data.\\n\\nI'm also planning the other test cases: REQ-05 needs a token-2022 transfer attempt from the owner's ATA to another wallet's ATA (building that via the associated-token-account and token-2022 instruction interfaces) and verifying it fails, plus checking balance, supply, and mint authority afterward. REQ-06 covers idempotency — a repeat call with the same id should fail while a different id should succeed.\\n\\nI still need to verify REQ-07 (config starts at life_stage Born and memory_epoch 0) and confirm that a failed instruction leaves config state completely unchanged, then write all these tests out.\\n\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Compatibility is confirmed at the API level, so I'm writing the program now. First I'm replacing the scaffold's counter code with the real instruction."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TZCQts1LWMR9ByUybUcfdg","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/opadmin/soulbound/programs/soulbound && rm -rf programs/soulbound/src/instructions programs/soulbound/src/constants.rs tests/src/test_initialize.rs\nmkdir -p programs/soulbound/src/instructions tests/fixtures\ncat > programs/soulbound/Cargo.toml <<'EOF'\n[package]\nname = \"soulbound\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"SOULBOUND: verifiable on-chain character birth\"\nedition.workspace = true\nrust-version.workspace = true\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"lib\"]\nname = \"soulbound\"\n\n[features]\ndefault = []\ncpi = [\"no-entrypoint\"]\nno-entrypoint = []\nno-log-ix-name = []\nidl-build = [\"anchor-lang/idl-build\", \"anchor-spl/idl-build\"]\nanchor-debug = []\ncustom-heap = []\ncustom-panic = []\n\n[dependencies]\nanchor-lang = \"=1.2.1\"\nanchor-spl = { version = \"=1.2.1\", features = [\"token_2022\", \"token_2022_extensions\", \"associated_token\"] }\nmpl-core = { version = \"=0.12.1\", features = [\"borsh-v1\"] }\n\n[lints.rust]\nunexpected_cfgs = { level = \"warn\", check-cfg = ['cfg(target_os, values(\"solana\"))'] }\nEOF\ncat > programs/soulbound/src/error.rs <<'EOF'\nuse anchor_lang::prelude::*;\n\n#[error_code]\npub enum SoulboundError {\n    #[msg(\"Trait vector exceeds the maximum allowed length\")]\n    TraitVectorTooLong,\n    #[msg(\"Arithmetic overflow\")]\n    MathOverflow,\n}\nEOF\ncat > programs/soulbound/src/state.rs <<'EOF'\nuse anchor_lang::prelude::*;\n\npub const CHARACTER_SEED: &[u8] = b\"character\";\npub const MAX_TRAIT_VECTOR_LEN: usize = 128;\npub const CHARACTER_NAME: &str = \"SOULBOUND Character\";\n\n#[derive(AnchorSerialize, AnchorDeserialize, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, InitSpace, Debug)]\npub enum LifeStage {\n    Born,\n}\n\nimpl LifeStage {\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &'static str {\n        match self {\n            LifeStage::Born => \"born\",\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[account]\n#[derive(InitSpace)]\npub struct CharacterConfig {\n    pub owner: Pubkey,\n    pub character_id: u64,\n    pub runtime_signer: Pubkey,\n    pub asset: Pubkey,\n    pub receipt_mint: Pubkey,\n    pub memory_epoch: u64,\n    pub life_stage: LifeStage,\n    pub bump: u8,\n}\nEOF\ncat > programs/soulbound/src/instructions.rs <<'EOF'\npub mod initialize_character;\npub use initialize_character::*;\nEOF\ncat > programs/soulbound/src/lib.rs <<'EOF'\npub mod error;\npub mod instructions;\npub mod state;\n\nuse anchor_lang::prelude::*;\n\npub use instructions::*;\npub use state::*;\n\ndeclare_id!(\"BdswGigVwzuRjcbj2XMsNHTGB37pCaPQquq8v1tAqJZd\");\n\n#[program]\npub mod soulbound {\n    use super::*;\n\n    /// REQ-01..03, 05..07: birth of a character.\n    pub fn initialize_character(\n        ctx: Context<InitializeCharacter>,\n        character_id: u64,\n        runtime_signer: Pubkey,\n        trait_vector: String,\n    ) -> Result<()> {\n        instructions::initialize_character::handle(ctx, character_id, runtime_signer, trait_vector)\n    }\n}\nEOF\ncat > programs/soulbound/src/instructions/initialize_character.rs <<'EOF'\nuse anchor_lang::prelude::*;\nuse anchor_lang::system_program::{create_account, CreateAccount};\nuse anchor_spl::associated_token::{self, AssociatedToken, Create};\nuse anchor_spl::token_2022::spl_token_2022::{extension::ExtensionType, state::Mint};\nuse anchor_spl::token_2022::{self, MintTo, SetAuthority, Token2022};\nuse anchor_spl::token_2022_extensions::{non_transferable_mint_initialize, NonTransferableMintInitialize};\nuse mpl_core::instructions::CreateV1Builder;\nuse mpl_core::types::{Attribute, Attributes, Plugin, PluginAuthorityPair};\n\nuse crate::error::SoulboundError;\nuse crate::state::*;\n\n#[derive(Accounts)]\n#[instruction(character_id: u64)]\npub struct InitializeCharacter<'info> {\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub owner: Signer<'info>,\n\n    // REQ-01 / REQ-06: canonical PDA; `init` fails if this (owner, id) already exists.\n    #[account(\n        init,\n        payer = owner,\n        space = 8 + CharacterConfig::INIT_SPACE,\n        seeds = [CHARACTER_SEED, owner.key().as_ref(), &character_id.to_le_bytes()],\n        bump\n    )]\n    pub config: Account<'info, CharacterConfig>,\n\n    /// New Core asset keypair (signs its own creation).\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub asset: Signer<'info>,\n\n    /// New Token-2022 receipt mint keypair.\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub receipt_mint: Signer<'info>,\n\n    /// CHECK: created by the associated-token program inside this instruction.\n    #[account(mut)]\n    pub owner_receipt_ata: UncheckedAccount<'info>,\n\n    /// CHECK: pinned to the Metaplex Core program id.\n    #[account(address = mpl_core::ID)]\n    pub core_program: UncheckedAccount<'info>,\n\n    pub token_program: Program<'info, Token2022>,\n    pub associated_token_program: Program<'info, AssociatedToken>,\n    pub system_program: Program<'info, System>,\n}\n\npub fn handle(\n    ctx: Context<InitializeCharacter>,\n    character_id: u64,\n    runtime_signer: Pubkey,\n    trait_vector: String,\n) -> Result<()> {\n    require!(\n        trait_vector.len() <= MAX_TRAIT_VECTOR_LEN,\n        SoulboundError::TraitVectorTooLong\n    );\n\n    let owner_key = ctx.accounts.owner.key();\n    let bump = ctx.bumps.config;\n\n    // REQ-07: config state.\n    let cfg = &mut ctx.accounts.config;\n    cfg.owner = owner_key;\n    cfg.character_id = character_id;\n    cfg.runtime_signer = runtime_signer;\n    cfg.asset = ctx.accounts.asset.key();\n    cfg.receipt_mint = ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.key();\n    cfg.memory_epoch = 0;\n    cfg.life_stage = LifeStage::Born;\n    cfg.bump = bump;\n    let life_stage = cfg.life_stage.as_str();\n\n    let id_bytes = character_id.to_le_bytes();\n    let seeds: &[&[u8]] = &[CHARACTER_SEED, owner_key.as_ref(), &id_bytes, &[bump]];\n    let signer_seeds = &[seeds];\n\n    // REQ-05: Token-2022 receipt. NonTransferable MUST be initialized before InitializeMint.\n    let space = ExtensionType::try_calculate_account_len::<Mint>(&[ExtensionType::NonTransferable])\n        .map_err(|_| error!(SoulboundError::MathOverflow))?;\n    let lamports = Rent::get()?.minimum_balance(space);\n    create_account(\n        CpiContext::new(\n            ctx.accounts.system_program.key(),\n            CreateAccount {\n                from: ctx.accounts.owner.to_account_info(),\n                to: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info(),\n            },\n        ),\n        lamports,\n        space as u64,\n        &ctx.accounts.token_program.key(),\n    )?;\n    non_transferable_mint_initialize(CpiContext::new(\n        ctx.accounts.token_program.key(),\n        NonTransferableMintInitialize {\n            token_program_id: ctx.accounts.token_program.to_account_info(),\n            mint: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info(),\n        },\n    ))?;\n    token_2022::initialize_mint2(\n        CpiContext::new(\n            ctx.accounts.token_program.key(),\n            token_2022::InitializeMint2 { mint: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info() },\n        ),\n        0,\n        &ctx.accounts.config.key(),\n        None,\n    )?;\n    associated_token::create(CpiContext::new(\n        ctx.accounts.associated_token_program.key(),\n        Create {\n            payer: ctx.accounts.owner.to_account_info(),\n            associated_token: ctx.accounts.owner_receipt_ata.to_account_info(),\n            authority: ctx.accounts.owner.to_account_info(),\n            mint: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info(),\n            system_program: ctx.accounts.system_program.to_account_info(),\n            token_program: ctx.accounts.token_program.to_account_info(),\n        },\n    ))?;\n    token_2022::mint_to(\n        CpiContext::new_with_signer(\n            ctx.accounts.token_program.key(),\n            MintTo {\n                mint: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info(),\n                to: ctx.accounts.owner_receipt_ata.to_account_info(),\n                authority: ctx.accounts.config.to_account_info(),\n            },\n            signer_seeds,\n        ),\n        1,\n    )?;\n    // Exactly one receipt ever: drop the mint authority.\n    token_2022::set_authority(\n        CpiContext::new_with_signer(\n            ctx.accounts.token_program.key(),\n            SetAuthority {\n                current_authority: ctx.accounts.config.to_account_info(),\n                account_or_mint: ctx.accounts.receipt_mint.to_account_info(),\n            },\n            signer_seeds,\n        ),\n        anchor_spl::token_2022::spl_token_2022::instruction::AuthorityType::MintTokens,\n        None,\n    )?;\n\n    // REQ-02 / REQ-03: Core asset with genesis Attributes; config PDA is update authority.\n    let attr = |k: &str, v: &str| Attribute { key: k.to_string(), value: v.to_string() };\n    let attributes = Attributes {\n        attribute_list: vec![\n            attr(\"life_stage\", life_stage),\n            attr(\"mood\", \"curious\"),\n            attr(\"memory_epoch\", \"0\"),\n            attr(\"trait_vector\", &trait_vector),\n        ],\n    };\n    let ix = CreateV1Builder::new()\n        .asset(ctx.accounts.asset.key())\n        .payer(owner_key)\n        .owner(Some(owner_key))\n        .update_authority(Some(ctx.accounts.config.key()))\n        .system_program(ctx.accounts.system_program.key())\n        .name(CHARACTER_NAME.to_string())\n        .uri(String::new())\n        .plugins(vec![PluginAuthorityPair {\n            plugin: Plugin::Attributes(attributes),\n            authority: None,\n        }])\n        .instruction();\n    anchor_lang::solana_program::program::invoke(\n        &ix,\n        &[\n            ctx.accounts.asset.to_account_info(),\n            ctx.accounts.config.to_account_info(),\n            ctx.accounts.owner.to_account_info(),\n            ctx.accounts.system_program.to_account_info(),\n            ctx.accounts.core_program.to_account_info(),\n        ],\n    )?;\n    Ok(())\n}\nEOF\ncat > Anchor.toml <<'EOF'\n[toolchain]\n\n[features]\nresolution = true\nskip-lint = false\n\n[programs.localnet]\nsoulbound = \"BdswGigVwzuRjcbj2XMsNHTGB37pCaPQquq8v1tAqJZd\"\n\n[provider]\ncluster = \"localnet\"\nwallet = \"~/.config/solana/id.json\"\n\n[scripts]\ntest = \"cargo test -p tests -- --nocapture\"\n\n[hooks]\nEOF\ngrep -n \"pub use\\|pub mod\" /dev/null; echo ok"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"surplus","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","usage":{"input":3875,"output":7473,"cacheRead":48367,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":59715,"cost":{"input":0.00775,"output":0.07473,"cacheRead":0.0048367,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0873167}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793163235757,"responseId":"msg_011CgU38szyY9NpnBm5G6rfj","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":42498,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
