{"type":"message","id":"a3a81859","parentId":"a1da4493","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:32:47.027Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Send devnet SOL to:\n\n```\nCdvYdEJUk4gxXhz53v7SAKggzfyKx5ho85uRhhvnMKs1\n```\n\n**How much:** 3 SOL is comfortable (deploy needs ~1.8 SOL for the program account + buffer, plus fees and the genesis character mint). 2 SOL is the bare minimum for just the deploy.\n\nThat keypair is fresh, generated just now, and lives at `~/.config/solana/id.json` — it's the deploy authority and will pay for the genesis character. It's outside the repo, so it can't get committed.\n\nWhile I wait, here's where everything stands:\n\n**Done and verified locally**\n- `anchor build` clean, `target/idl/soulbound.json` present\n- LiteSVM suite: 5/5 green, one test per REQ (01, 02, 03, 05, 06, 07)\n- Negative tests assert *exact* error codes, not just \"something failed\": non-transferable transfer → `Custom(37)` = Token-2022 `NonTransferable`; duplicate id → `Custom(0)` = `AccountAlreadyInUse`; over-long trait vector → `Custom(6000)` = `TraitVectorTooLong`\n- Mutation-checked: deleting the NonTransferable init makes REQ-05 fail, so the test isn't vacuous\n\n**The compatibility gate you asked about — passed, no downgrade needed**\n- anchor-lang 1.2.1 + mpl-core 0.12.1 + spl-token-2022-interface 3 resolve and compile cleanly\n- One real catch: mpl-core's optional `anchor` feature would pull in anchor-lang **0.31/0.32** alongside 1.2.1. I left that feature off and use mpl-core's plain builders plus `invoke` — the versions stay unified\n- Pinned `anchor-lang =1.2.1`, `mpl-core =0.12.1`, LiteSVM `0.18.1`, Agave `4.3.2` — I'll write these into `docs/devnet.md` at deploy time\n\n**One ticket-level conflict I need you or AdaL to resolve**\n\nThe ticket's verification command is `anchor test --skip-local-validator`, which in Anchor 1.2.1 still tries to *deploy to a live cluster* at `127.0.0.1:8899` and needs `ANCHOR_WALLET`. It does not run the LiteSVM suite. My suite runs via `cargo test -p tests` (wired as `[scripts] test` in `Anchor.toml`). So that exact command will never prove the REQ criteria — it needs a validator, not LiteSVM. I've left the command untouched since `tickets/` is off-limits to me; flag it and I'll adapt, or AdaL amends the ticket.\n\n**Also worth knowing now:** the SBF toolchain ships rustc `1.95.0-dev`, so the program crate must keep `rust-version = \"1.89.0\"` while the test crate needs `1.97.1` (LiteSVM/Agave requirement). Bumping the workspace-wide version silently breaks `anchor build` while `cargo test` still passes — I found that the hard way and split the pins.\n\nTwo things I can't finish without you: the funded deploy, and a real genesis mint on devnet (needs the same funds). Ping me when the SOL lands and I'll deploy, mint, pin the ID in `docs/devnet.md`, and write up `audit/002-anchor-genesis-mint/`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"surplus","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","usage":{"input":107068,"output":1163,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":465,"totalTokens":108231,"cost":{"input":0.214136,"output":0.011630000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.225766}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1793165527662,"responseId":"gen-1793165533-gaEy76u8MsOJ4cfCHNrL","rawStopReason":"stop","durationMs":39365,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
