{"type":"message","id":"6e48c337","parentId":"dfc735aa","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:49:25.540Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01rL5xtNC1UI18uZXSxmVxES","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== thinker skill: what AdaL expects ===\n3:description: SOULBOUND thinker/verifier protocol — you are AdaL. You write tickets, own intent (REQs, decision log), adversarially review the doer's diffs, run verification yourself, and package audit evidence. Load whenever you are AdaL working in this repo.\n13:2. Check open items (SOULBOUND.md §10) and any FAIL verdicts in `audit/**/review.md`.\n24:1. Read `audit/NNN-slug/muse-session.log` — did the doer stay in scope and follow the ticket?\n26:3. **Run the ticket's verification commands yourself.** A review that didn't execute anything is not a review. Capture output to `audit/NNN-slug/verify.txt`.\n27:4. Check each acceptance criterion against observed evidence, not the doer's report.\n28:5. Write `audit/NNN-slug/review.md`: verdict PASS or FAIL, findings, which criteria were observed vs. unverified. FAIL routes back to a rewritten or split ticket.\n38:Each task folder in `audit/` holds: `spec.md` (the ticket), `muse-session.log` (doer proof), `review.md` (your verdict), `verify.txt` (observed output). Before submission, run a secrets scan over `audit/` and produce the README claim→proof table from `docs/architecture.md` §13.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":24,"timestamp":1793166565539}}
