{"type":"message","id":"23ad091d","parentId":"98068851","timestamp":"2026-10-28T05:50:30.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — AdaL will be missing the things that make the evidence reproducible. Three of them will actively strand her.\n\n## What she'll definitely lack\n\n**1. There is no Rust/Solana/Anchor on the host.**\n\n```\n$ command -v cargo anchor solana   → NONE on host\n```\n\nI used a Docker image I built (`sb-anchor:1.2.1`, 3.84 GB) plus a runner script at `/tmp/dk.sh`. `/tmp` is ephemeral. If AdaL opens a shell and runs the ticket's `anchor build`, she gets `command not found` — and will reasonably conclude the doer did nothing. The build recipe exists only in `/tmp/sbimg/Dockerfile`.\n\n**2. The whole test setup depends on that image.** `cargo test -p tests` needs host rustc ≥1.97.1 *and* the `tests/fixtures/mpl_core.so` fixture *and* the SBF toolchain for `anchor build`. None of it is a plain `pnpm install` away.\n\n**3. The deploy keypair is root-owned and unreadable by her.**\n\n```\n$ head /home/opadmin/.config/solana/id.json → Permission denied\n```\n\nDocker wrote it as root. AdaL can't read it, can't `solana program show` with it, can't re-mint. That's a real blocker, not a convenience issue.\n\n## What she *will* have\n\n`docs/devnet.md` is genuinely thorough — pinned versions, both tx signatures, every address, the toolchain split, the compatibility finding, and an honest note that the ticket's `anchor test --skip-local-validator` command doesn't do what the ticket claims. All the on-chain facts are independently re-verifiable by her through a plain HTTPS call to devnet, no toolchain needed.\n\nPlus the 16 source files, the 5-test suite, and my report.\n\n## What shipped nowhere\n\n- The `anchor program deploy` failure (`No random values implementation could be found`) — Node 18 vs Anchor's JS IDL step. I used `solana program deploy` instead. That reasoning is in this chat only.\n- The mutation test — I deleted the NonTransferable init and confirmed REQ-05 failed. Good evidence the tests aren't vacuous; invisible to her.\n- How `mpl_core.so` was obtained (`solana program dump`) — actually in `docs/devnet.md`, fine.\n- No `audit/002-anchor-genesis-mint/` exists. Her skill wants `muse-session.log` there, and I can't write it.\n\n## Fix it in about two minutes\n\nWant me to write a short operator note into the repo recording the build environment, so she can reproduce the suite without this conversation? I'd put it at `programs/soulbound/BUILD.md` — inside the ticket's \"Files in scope\" (`programs/soulbound/` is in scope, and this is part of the Anchor workspace), so it doesn't break the scope rule. It would carry the Dockerfile, the runner, the `solana program deploy` fallback, and the mutation-test result.\n\nSeparately, I should hand the keypair back to you: `sudo chown opadmin:opadmin /home/opadmin/.config/solana/id.json` — I can't do it, I have no sudo. Once that's done AdaL can verify the deploy herself.\n\nSay which you want, or I'll leave it here and you can relay the environment facts by hand."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"surplus","model":"claude-sonnet-5.5","usage":{"input":130484,"output":1124,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":450,"totalTokens":131608,"cost":{"input":0.260968,"output":0.011240000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.272208}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1793166604072,"responseId":"gen-1793166604-ix6siFRpuUWR8rTF8Dn4","rawStopReason":"stop","durationMs":26586,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
