{"type":"message","id":"beb4c28e","parentId":"a4fe0105","timestamp":"2026-10-28T06:04:28.659Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Facts confirmed. Writing the note now."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01vJEjWEc7LUdl9mJkxFThsG","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Building and verifying Ticket 002 (operator note for AdaL)\n\nWritten by the doer (pi) at the end of Ticket 002. This exists because the build\nenvironment is **not** the host shell: there is no `cargo`, `rustc`, `solana`, or `anchor`\ninstalled on the VPS. Every command below was actually run against this repo; nothing here\nis inferred from documentation.\n\n`docs/devnet.md` holds the on-chain pins (program ID, tx signatures, mint/asset addresses,\nversion pins). This file holds the *how to reproduce*.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Read this first: the host has no toolchain\n\n```console\n$ command -v cargo anchor solana\n# (no output — none of them exist on the host)\n```\n\nAll builds and tests ran inside a Docker image built for this ticket:\n\n```\nsb-anchor:1.2.1\n```\n\nIf you open a shell and run the ticket's `anchor build`, you will get `command not found`.\nThat is an environment fact, not evidence the work was not done.\n\n## 2. Rebuild the toolchain image (only needed if it is gone)\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /tmp/sbimg && cd /tmp/sbimg\ncat > Dockerfile <<'EOF'\nFROM rust:1-bookworm\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n    pkg-config libssl-dev libudev-dev clang llvm nodejs npm bzip2 \\\n && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\nRUN sh -c \"$(curl -sSfL https://release.anza.xyz/stable/install)\"\nENV PATH=\"/root/.local/share/solana/install/active_release/bin:/usr/local/cargo/bin:${PATH}\"\nRUN cargo install anchor-cli --version =1.2.1 --locked\nRUN solana --version && anchor --version\nEOF\ndocker build -t sb-anchor:1.2.1 .\n```\n\nIt yields `solana-cli 4.3.2` (client: Agave) and `anchor-cli 1.2.1`. The image is ~3.8 GB and\nthe `anchor-cli` compile takes several minutes.\n\n## 3. The runner used for every command in this ticket\n\n```bash\ncat > /tmp/dk.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\ndocker run --rm --user 0 -v sbcargo:/usr/local/cargo/registry \\\n  -v /home/opadmin/soulbound/programs/soulbound:/w \\\n  -v /home/opadmin/.config/solana:/root/.config/solana \\\n  -w /w sb-anchor:1.2.1 sh -c \"solana config set --url devnet \\\n  --keypair /root/.config/solana/id.json >/dev/null 2>&1; $1; \\\n  rc=\\$?; chown -R 1000:1000 /w 2>/dev/null; exit \\$rc\"\nEOF\nchmod +x /tmp/dk.sh\ndocker volume create sbcargo     # caches the cargo registry across runs\n```\n\n`--user 0` is needed because the image's toolchain lives under `/root`. The trailing\n`chown -R 1000:1000` is what keeps `target/` writable from the host afterwards.\n\n## 4. Reproduce the verification\n\n```bash\n# program + IDL  ->  target/deploy/soulbound.so , target/idl/soulbound.json\n/tmp/dk.sh 'cd /w && anchor build'\n\n# LiteSVM suite (REQ-01, 02, 03, 05, 06, 07). Needs target/deploy/soulbound.so\n# to exist first — the tests load it from disk.\n/tmp/dk.sh 'cd /w && cargo test -p tests -- --nocapture --test-threads=1'\n\n# program is executable on devnet (no toolchain required, works from the host)\ncurl -s -X POST https://api.devnet.solana.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"getAccountInfo\",\"params\":[\n      \"BdswGigVwzuRjcbj2XMsNHTGB37pCaPQquq8v1tAqJZd\",{\"encoding\":\"base64\"}]}'\n```\n\n## 5. Two gotchas that cost real time\n\n### The ticket's `anchor test --skip-local-validator` does not run LiteSVM\n\nWith anchor-cli 1.2.1 that command still tries to deploy to a live cluster:\n\n```\nDeploying cluster: http://127.0.0.1:8899\nUpgrade authority: /root/.config/solana/id.json\nDeploying program \"soulbound\"...\nProgram path: /w/target/deploy/soulbound.so...\nError: Unable to read keypair file (/root/.config/solana/id.json)\n```\n\nIt needs a validator and a wallet; it never executes `tests/`. The suite is Rust + litesvm,\nrun with `cargo test -p tests`. `Anchor.toml` wires `[scripts] test` to exactly that, so\n`anchor run test` works. **The ticket text still names the wrong command** — that is a\nticket amendment for AdaL, deliberately not edited by the doer.\n\n### `anchor program deploy` is broken in this image; use `solana program deploy`\n\n```\n[Error] No random values implementation could be found.\nError: Failed to initialize IDL\n```\n\nAnchor 1.2.1 shells out to a JS IDL step that fails against the Node 18 in the image. The\nworking deploy, using the same program keypair, is:\n\n```bash\n/tmp/dk.sh 'solana program deploy target/deploy/soulbound.so \\\n  --program-id target/deploy/soulbound-keypair.json --url devnet \\\n  --keypair /root/.config/solana/id.json'\n```\n\nThe program keypair (`target/deploy/soulbound-keypair.json`) is generated by `anchor init`\nand gitignored, so a rebuild must keep that file or the program ID changes.\n\n## 6. Rust version pins are deliberately split\n\n| Crate | `rust-version` | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| workspace + `programs/soulbound` | `1.89.0` | SBF toolchain ships `rustc 1.95.0-dev` |\n| `tests` | `1.97.1` | litesvm 0.18.1 / Agave 4.3.2 demand it |\n\nDo not \"tidy\" these into one value. Raising the workspace pin breaks `anchor build` with\n`error: rustc 1.95.0-dev is not supported ... soulbound@0.1.0 requires rustc 1.97.1`\nwhile `cargo test` keeps compiling — a silent, easy-to-miss failure.\n\n`rust-toolchain.toml` pins host channel `1.99.1` for the test crate.\n\n## 7. The Metaplex Core fixture\n\n`tests/fixtures/mpl_core.so` (856 KB) is a dump of the live Core program, so the suite\nexercises the real binary rather than a mock:\n\n```bash\nsolana program dump CoREENxT6tW1HoK8ypY1SxRMZTcVPm7R94rH4PZNhX7d \\\n  tests/fixtures/mpl_core.so --url devnet\n```\n\nmpl-core is pinned at `0.12.1` with **only** the `borsh-v1` feature. Do not enable its\n`anchor` feature: it pulls `anchor-lang 0.31`/`0.32` and `solana-program 2` under the same\ncrate name as our 1.2.1 / `solana-program 3`, silently splitting the Solana types. The CPI\nis driven with `CreateV1Builder::instruction()` + `solana_program::program::invoke` for\nexactly this reason. Rationale and the compatibility matrix are in `docs/devnet.md`.\n\n## 8. Deploy keypair permissions (action needed by the operator)\n\n`~/.config/solana/id.json` — deploy authority\n`CdvYdEJUk4gxXhz53v7SAKggzfyKx5ho85uRhhvnMKs1` — was created by Docker as `root`, so it is\n**not readable from the host shell**:\n\n```console\n$ cat /home/opadmin/.config/solana/id.json\nPermission denied\n```\n\nUntil ownership is fixed, host-side `solana` commands that need the signer will fail. One\nline, needs sudo:\n\n```bash\nsudo chown -R opadmin:opadmin /home/opadmin/.config/solana\nsudo chmod 600 /home/opadmin/.config/solana/id.json\n```\n\nThe keypair is intentionally outside the repo and must never be committed. Devnet only.\n\n## 9. A note on the test suite's strength\n\nThe five tests assert specific failure codes rather than merely \"it errored\":\n\n| REQ | Rejection asserted |\n|---|---|\n| REQ-05 | transfer → `InstructionError(0, Custom(37))` = Token-2022 `NonTransferable` |\n| REQ-06 | duplicate `character_id` → `Custom(0)` = `AccountAlreadyInUse` |\n| REQ-07 | 129-byte trait vector → `Custom(6000)` = `SoulboundError::TraitVectorTooLong` |\n\nREQ-05 was additionally mutation-checked during the session: with the\n`non_transferable_mint_initialize` CPI deleted from the handler, that test fails. It is\ndetecting the extension, not passing vacuously. This is a self-check by the doer, not a\nsubstitute for your independent run.\n\n## 10. What was not verified\n\n- `commit_memory_root`, `evolve_traits`, `crank_heartbeat` — out of scope (later tickets).\n- The Core Oracle plugin (REQ-04) — Ticket 005.\n- No `audit/002-anchor-genesis-mint/` exists; that is yours to populate. There is no\n  `muse-session.log` because the doer harness was pi, not Muse Code.\